    "result_text": "The people table now has a **Wharf** column showing each person's keel times four, or `n/a` when keel is n/a. `bin/e2e` passes.\n\n- **Server:** `PersonView.java` works out `wharf` the same way as the other values based on keel, and its comment block describes it.\n- **Front end:** `people.service.ts` has the new `wharf` field, and `people-list.ts` adds the column with `data-testid=\"concept-wharf\"`. I made the empty footer cells one column wider so the footer rows still span the whole table.\n- **Stored data:** wharf is calculated, not stored, so the schema and the test seed/read-back endpoints didn't need changing.\n\nI found one inconsistency outside this change and left it alone: for `beam`, the Java comment and code say \"keel times three\", but the front-end comment says \"keel times two\". The app displays the server's value, so only the front-end comment is wrong \u2014 but which one was intended is worth checking.",
